#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from using Qiskit Pulse to fractional gates to execute single and "
"two-qubit rotations"
msgstr ""
"Mag-migrate mula sa paggamit ng Qiskit Pulse patungong fractional gates para"
" isagawa ang single at two-qubit na mga rotasyon"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from Qiskit Pulse to fractional gates"
msgstr "Mag-migrate mula sa Qiskit Pulse patungong fractional gates"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from Qiskit Pulse to fractional gates {#migrate-from-qiskit-pulse-"
"to-fractional-gates}"
msgstr ""
"Mag-migrate mula sa Qiskit Pulse patungong fractional gates {#migrate-from-"
"qiskit-pulse-to-fractional-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the introduction of [fractional gates](../guides/fractional-gates), "
"pulse-level control on all IBM Quantum&reg; processors has been deprecated "
"and will be removed in early 2025. Additionally, the `qiskit.pulse` module "
"has been deprecated as of the Qiskit SDK v1.3.0 and will be removed in "
"Qiskit SDK v2.0.0. This change was motivated by our ongoing focus on "
"utility-scale experiments and support for users exploring applications that "
"might lead to quantum advantage.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagpapakilala ng [fractional gates](../guides/fractional-gates), ang "
"pulse-level na kontrol sa lahat ng IBM Quantum&reg; processor ay na-"
"deprecate na at aalisin sa unang bahagi ng 2025. Bukod dito, ang "
"`qiskit.pulse` module ay na-deprecate na simula sa Qiskit SDK v1.3.0 at "
"aalisin sa Qiskit SDK v2.0.0. Naudyukan ang pagbabagong ito ng aming patuloy"
" na pagtuon sa utility-scale na mga eksperimento at suporta para sa mga "
"gumagamit na nagsa-explore ng mga aplikasyon na maaaring humantong sa "
"quantum advantage.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Execute single- and two-qubit rotations directly with fractional gates "
"{#execute-single-and-two-qubit-rotations-directly-with-fractional-gates}"
msgstr ""
"Direktang isagawa ang single- at two-qubit na mga rotasyon gamit ang "
"fractional gates {#execute-single-and-two-qubit-rotations-directly-with-"
"fractional-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most common use-case of pulse-level control was to build custom pulse "
"schedules that modify the `ECR` or `RX` pulses to directly execute single- "
"and two-qubit rotations. The typical process was to use the "
"`RXCalibrationBuilder` and `RZXCalibrationBuilder` (or "
"`RZXCalibrationBuilderNoEcho`) and add either a `RXGate` or `RZXGate` "
"instruction to a QPU's `target`, then build a transpilation pipeline "
"containing the calibration builder passes to calibrate the single- and two-"
"qubit rotations for a specified angle. In the background this created a "
"*calibration*, which is a map between a `ScheduleBlock` and a gate in a "
"`QuantumCircuit`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinakakaraniwang gamit ng pulse-level na kontrol ay ang pagbuo ng mga "
"custom na pulse schedule na nagbabago ng `ECR` o `RX` na mga pulse para "
"direktang isagawa ang single- at two-qubit na mga rotasyon. Ang karaniwang "
"proseso ay ang paggamit ng `RXCalibrationBuilder` at `RZXCalibrationBuilder`"
" (o `RZXCalibrationBuilderNoEcho`) at ang pagdaragdag ng `RXGate` o "
"`RZXGate` na instruksyon sa `target` ng isang QPU, pagkatapos ay bumuo ng "
"transpilation pipeline na naglalaman ng mga calibration builder pass para "
"i-calibrate ang single- at two-qubit na mga rotasyon para sa isang tinukoy "
"na anggulo. Sa background, lumilikha ito ng *calibration*, na isang mapa sa "
"pagitan ng isang `ScheduleBlock` at isang gate sa isang `QuantumCircuit`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can now accomplish this on Heron processors using the new "
"`use_fractional_gates` flag. As specified in the [fractional gates "
"guide](/guides/fractional-gates), both $R_X(\\theta)$ and $R_ZZ(\\theta)$ "
"must be loaded using this flag, which returns a backend whose `Target` "
"attribute contains information about these gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magagawa mo na ngayon ito sa mga Heron processor gamit ang bagong "
"`use_fractional_gates` na flag. Tulad ng tinukoy sa [fractional gates "
"guide](/guides/fractional-gates), ang parehong $R_X(\\theta)$ at "
"$R_ZZ(\\theta)$ ay kailangang i-load gamit ang flag na ito, na nagbabalik ng"
" backend na ang `Target` attribute ay naglalaman ng impormasyon tungkol sa "
"mga gate na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use Qiskit Dynamics {#use-qiskit-dynamics}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang Qiskit Dynamics {#use-qiskit-dynamics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit.pulse` module contained much more functionality than just "
"executing single and two-qubit rotations more efficiently. Much of the "
"control over device physics can be modeled using the [Qiskit "
"Dynamics](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-dynamics/) package found"
" in the Qiskit Ecosystem. In particular, the package has its own analogous "
"representation of many of the features provided by `qiskit.pulse` in the "
"form of a `qiskit_dynamics.signals` module.  The documentation of this "
"package contains a few tutorials which may be helpful:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `qiskit.pulse` module ay naglalaman ng mas maraming functionality kaysa "
"sa simpleng pagsasagawa ng single at two-qubit na mga rotasyon nang mas "
"mahusay. Malaking bahagi ng kontrol sa physics ng device ay maaaring i-model"
" gamit ang [Qiskit Dynamics](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-"
"dynamics/) package na matatagpuan sa Qiskit Ecosystem. Sa partikular, ang "
"package ay may sariling katumbas na representasyon ng marami sa mga feature "
"na ibinibigay ng `qiskit.pulse` sa anyo ng isang `qiskit_dynamics.signals` "
"module. Ang dokumentasyon ng package na ito ay naglalaman ng ilang mga "
"tutorial na maaaring makatulong:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Simulating Qiskit Pulse Schedules](https://qiskit-"
"community.github.io/qiskit-dynamics/tutorials/qiskit_pulse.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"[Simulating Qiskit Pulse Schedules](https://qiskit-"
"community.github.io/qiskit-dynamics/tutorials/qiskit_pulse.html)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
